Mesa's software OpenGL fallback already prefers the fast "llvmpipe" rasterizer
automatically, except on a CPU the app thinks might be a conservative
virtual-machine CPU model prone to a known llvmpipe hang (missing the SSE4.1
instruction set). If you've confirmed this specific machine doesn't actually
hit that hang and want llvmpipe's speed anyway, rename this file to
".force-mesa-performance" — remove the ".sample" extension. Only the file's
name and location matter; this text is never read by the app.
